  "id": "Compound::DB01167 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Itraconazole, a broad-spectrum antifungal agent, is shown to bind to Cyp2b6 and Cyp2d6, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the cytochrome P450 system and are known to catalyze the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that generates bioactive lipid mediators. The observed relationship between Itraconazole and Cyp2e1 suggests that the drug may inhibit the activity of Cyp2e1 through a mechanism involving the binding of Itraconazole to Cyp2b6 or Cyp2d6, which in turn may affect the overall metabolic capacity of Cyp2e1. The shared pathway of arachidonic acid metabolism across these enzymes implies that Itraconazole may exert its effects by modulating the activity of Cyp2e1, potentially through competitive inhibition or by altering the expression or function of the enzyme. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and biologically plausible mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Itraconazole and Cyp2e1.",
